# Performance

Measure before optimizing and protect constrained devices by default.

- Stream the raw source; never load the complete local dataset into memory.
- Publish compact, versioned query chunks and summaries, with detail shards
  loaded only on demand.
- Support validated HTTP range and conditional requests where artifact access
  benefits from them; keep cache keys version-aware.
- Run filtering, sorting, search suggestions, pagination, and export in the
  browser Web Worker, not on the React render thread.
- Keep Worker messages compact and versioned; use transferable data where it
  produces a measured benefit.
- Bound concurrency, memory, response sizes, and export work.
- Avoid request waterfalls and duplicate artifact downloads. Let TanStack Query
  own remote cache and request lifecycle.
- Diagnose build or runtime regressions from observed evidence, fix
  incrementally, and rerun only the focused check needed for the changed area.
